1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:11,574
The Medical board is the staff’s shared view of injuries, rehab and what needs reviewing today.

2
00:00:11,574 --> 00:00:18,414
Tom felt his hamstring during sprints. Open Injuries, then Declare.

3
00:00:18,414 --> 00:00:23,640
Pick the player, the type and the zone…

4
00:00:23,641 --> 00:00:36,667
…then the side, how severe it is and whether he can train or play.

5
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:42,196
Add an estimated return date and a note for the staff.

6
00:00:42,196 --> 00:00:47,633
Declare. The injury is shared with the whole staff instantly.

7
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:54,730
Open an injury to follow it: days out, severity, estimated return and progress. Here, Maxime’s knee.

8
00:00:54,730 --> 00:01:01,403
Recovery steps take him back to the group. Tick a step off when it’s done.

9
00:01:01,403 --> 00:01:06,943
Availability is set here too: unavailable, training only, or fit to play.

10
00:01:06,943 --> 00:01:15,933
Back on the board, Availability shows who can be selected. Tom and Maxime are out — and left off call-ups automatically.
